                <pb facs="0008" n="1" sameAs="frus:frus1937v03/pg1"/>

                <head>Chapter I: January 1–July 7, 1937</head>
                <p>Deterioration of Japan’s foreign relations as result of developments in 1936;
                    aftermath of Generalissimo Chiang Kai-shek’s release from kidnaping at Sian;
                    restatement of policy by new Foreign Ministers at Tokyo and Nanking; review of
                    American interest in China, March 13; Nanking-Moscow understanding (reported
                    March 26); negotiations between Nanking Government and Chinese Communist
                    leaders; Japanese Foreign Office effort to secure understanding with United
                    Kingdom as to China; continuing deadlock in Chinese-Japanese relations</p>

























































































































